# Prediction output. `outputs/` is also where the native Protenix CLI puts its
# compile cache when no directory is given.
outputs/
foldjax-outputs/

# Model weights, in every format the six backends publish or convert to.
#
# No weights are distributed with this software, and AlphaFold 3's parameters
# may not be redistributed at all, so an accidental `git add -A` here is a
# licence violation rather than a mistake to amend away. A checkout with a
# `.foldjax/` directory keeps its store there (`~/.cache/foldjax` otherwise, and
# `$FOLDJAX_HOME` over both), so the store is inside the working tree by default
# on a development machine, and these are the names it writes.
#
# Every pattern below was checked against `git ls-files` first: each matches
# zero tracked files today. Adding a `.pt` test fixture later would need
# `git add -f`, which is the intended trade.
*.apkl
*.bin
*.ckpt
*.jax
*.pkl
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.tar
# The CCD dictionary and its RDKit cache, shared by protenix and opendde.
# Named rather than blanket-ignoring `*.cif`, which is also the format every
# prediction writes and a plausible test fixture.
components.cif*

# The store itself: `paths.foldjax_home()` returns this directory when it
# exists. Only the nested directory is ignored -- a FOLDJAX_HOME at the
# repository root would put its `assets/` alongside the tracked one that holds
# this project's logos.
.foldjax/

# `*.npz` and `*.a3m` are deliberately absent. Four `data/*.npz` files are
# package data the wheel must ship, two more are test fixtures, and
# `examples/uniref90_hits.a3m` is a runnable example -- ignoring either
# extension would hide tracked files. Store copies land under `.foldjax/`.

# agent session state, not part of the project
.omc/
.oms/
_archive/
src/foldjax/models/alphafold3/_upstream/alphafold3/**/*.so
src/foldjax/models/alphafold3/_upstream/alphafold3/**/*.pickle
